            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"The ultimate archetype of extreme human wickedness, unrepentant sin (often specifically associated with sexual immorality), and sudden, total divine judgment.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Genesis 18-19\",\"Jude 1:7\",\"2 Peter 2:6\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Gross inhospitality, arrogance, and social injustice, specifically the failure to help the poor and needy.\",\"basis\":[\"Ezekiel 16:49-50\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The rejection of God's messengers and the gospel, serving as a baseline for comparing the severity of future judgment.\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 10:14-15\",\"Luke 10:12\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Proverbial absolute destruction, total desolation, or a barren wasteland representing the consequences of divine wrath.\",\"basis\":[\"Isaiah 1:9\",\"Isaiah 13:19\",\"Deuteronomy 29:23\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"While traditional interpretations often emphasize sexual immorality based on Jude and Genesis 19, modern scholarship frequently highlights inhospitality and social injustice based on Ezekiel 16. Despite debates over their primary sin, their function as a universal symbol for absolute divine judgment against wickedness is highly settled.\"}",
